//! lotus/stereo_center_clip.rye -- ALES141: the center clipper carried into stereo, ONE SHARED DEAD ZONE, opening the dead-zone corner of the stereo NONLINEAR class. ALES87 named `center_clip` -- silence the quiet
//! middle, pass the loud, y = if |x| ≤ t then 0 else x: the mirror of ALES132's hard clip, which caps the LOUD extremes at a ceiling. Where the clip flattens everything past ±ceil, the center clip zeros everything
//! within ±t and passes the rest UNCHANGED; run together in stereo they keep only the band t < |x| ≤ ceil. Yet a Lotus master is a StereoClip (ALES10), two Clips heard together whose defining invariant is that
//! LEFT and RIGHT hold the SAME length. This rung carries the center clip into stereo the plain way: run ALES87's proven mono `center_clip` on each channel with the SAME threshold, so one dead zone lands on BOTH
//! speakers together.
//!
//! Where the crush (ALES136) and the tube (ALES135) are NOT odd and break the inter-channel antisymmetry, the center clipper IS odd -- |−x| = |x|, so center_clip(−x) = −center_clip(x). That is this rung's
//! distinguishing law in the stereo field: an OUT-OF-PHASE master (right the exact negation of left) center-clipped through the same threshold comes back STILL out of phase (right = −left), because the dead-zone
//! map is symmetric about zero -- the mirror the not-odd siblings broke. A 1:2 master keeps its ratio on the passed samples (both silenced together in the dead zone, both passed together above it), and an
//! identical-channel master stays identical.
//!
//! The rule, stated once: the center clip is EXACT for every i16 with NO rail edge and NO saturate -- the only values written are 0 (the quiet middle silenced) and the untouched input (the loud passed). The magnitude
//! is taken in i32 inside ALES87 so |sample_min| = 32768 is representable, one past the positive rail. It carries ONE parameter, the threshold magnitude, and names TWO faults. Refuse BadThreshold (a threshold outside
//! [0, sample_max]) and BadRange (a span outside the samples) BEFORE either channel is mutated -- each fault depends only on the shared threshold or the shared length, so each check is made ONCE up front, and a refusal
//! never center-clips one channel and leaves the other whole; otherwise center_clip both channels over [start, start+count) with the same `thresh` via ALES87's `center_clip`. CenterClipError reused whole -- the stereo
//! lift adds no fault.
//!
//! The crux -- four laws. THE STEREO CENTER-CLIP LAW: each channel equals ALES87's mono `center_clip` with the same threshold over the same span byte for byte -- every quiet sample (|x| ≤ t) silenced to 0, every louder
//! sample passed unchanged, no rail edge. THE BALANCE / LENGTH LAW: left.len == right.len after the edit and both hold their starting length (a center clip writes values only). THE PER-CHANNEL ODD LAW (held in
//! stereo): the center clipper is odd (|−x| = |x|), so a shared dead zone HOLDS the inter-channel antisymmetry -- an out-of-phase master comes back STILL out of phase (right = −left), the mirror the crush and tube
//! broke; yet per channel every output is either 0 or exactly its input, the map is idempotent (twice equals once), a 1:2 master keeps its ratio on the passed samples, an identical-channel master stays identical, and
//! thresh = 0 is the identity. THE ATOMICITY / DEGENERATE LAW: any refusal (BadThreshold, BadRange) leaves BOTH channels byte for byte untouched and still balanced; thresh = 0 the identity on both, count = 0 the
//! identity on both.
//!
//! Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus - the creative suite) - waymark ALES - rung ALES141.
//! Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-042021_fill-ales141-lotus-stereo-center-clip.md
//! Stands on: lotus/center_clip.rye (ALES87) -- the mono center clipper run once per channel, y = if |x| ≤ t then 0 else x with no rail edge; lotus/stereo_crush.rye (ALES136) -- the not-odd sibling whose
//! antisymmetry-break this rung mirrors by HOLDING it; lotus/pan.rye (ALES10) -- the StereoClip (two mono Clips, left/right) and its balance invariant; lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2) -- the Clip, its buf/len/samples,
//! sample_min/max.
//!
//! HONEST SCOPE -- software only, purely LOCAL. Two bounded in-process i16 Clips (left, right) on one bench, siloed to lotus/. It changes sample VALUES only through ALES87's own center_clip, each output either silence
//! or exactly its input, never a length; the shape is a static dead-zone threshold on instantaneous magnitude, memoryless (no attack/release, no envelope, no anti-aliasing). No saturate is owed -- the only values
//! written are 0 and the legal input. No real sample rate, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no real speaker.
//!
//!   env RYE_ZIG=vendor/zig-toolchain/zig rye/bin/rye run lotus/stereo_center_clip.rye selftest

const std = @import("std");
const assert = std.debug.assert;
const print = std.debug.print;

const timeline = @import("timeline.rye");
const pan = @import("pan.rye");
const center_clip = @import("center_clip.rye");

pub const stereo_center_clip_version = "20260815.042021";

/// Stereo center-clip's faults are exactly ALES87's own `CenterClipError` -- `BadThreshold` (a threshold outside [0, sample_max]) and `BadRange` (a span outside the samples) -- reused by name, since the stereo lift
/// adds no new fault: it only runs the same center_clip on each channel after one shared validation.
pub const StereoCenterClipError = center_clip.CenterClipError;

/// Center-clip `[start, start+count)` in BOTH channels of `sc` with the same `thresh`, the SAME dead zone on each, running ALES87's proven mono `center_clip`. Each sample whose magnitude is at most `thresh` becomes
/// `0` (the quiet middle silenced), and every louder sample passes byte-for-byte -- y = if |x| ≤ thresh then 0 else x. Exact for every i16 with no rail edge (the only values written are 0 and the untouched input), so
/// no saturate is owed. `thresh = 0` is the identity. Validates both channels once against the shared threshold and length before either is mutated: refuses `BadThreshold` / `BadRange`, both channels untouched.
/// Values only -- never the length; the two channels leave balanced.
pub fn stereo_center_clip(sc: *pan.StereoClip, start: u32, count: u32, thresh: i32) StereoCenterClipError!void {
    // invariant: the two channels enter balanced -- the defining StereoClip invariant, the ground the edit preserves.
    assert(sc.left.len == sc.right.len);

    // invariant: the threshold and span are legal -- refused by name before any write, so a refusal never center-clips one channel and leaves the other whole. The threshold check depends only on the shared magnitude
    // bound; the span check on the shared length. These mirror ALES87's own guards exactly, so each mono center_clip below is pre-validated to succeed.
    if (thresh < 0) return error.BadThreshold;
    if (thresh > @as(i32, timeline.sample_max)) return error.BadThreshold;
    const len: u32 = sc.left.len;
    if (start > len) return error.BadRange;
    if (count > len - start) return error.BadRange;

    // Every check passed and holds identically for both channels, so each mono center_clip is pre-validated to succeed -- no refusal can land between the two channel edits. The SAME dead zone on each.
    try center_clip.center_clip(&sc.left, start, count, thresh);
    try center_clip.center_clip(&sc.right, start, count, thresh);

    // invariant: the channels leave balanced -- a center clip writes values only, so each channel holds its starting length and the stereo image stays aligned in time.
    assert(sc.left.len == sc.right.len);
    assert(sc.left.len <= sc.left.buf.len and sc.right.len <= sc.right.buf.len);
}

// --- selftest: THE STEREO CENTER-CLIP LAW -- each channel equals ALES87's mono center_clip with the same threshold over the same span byte for byte; THE BALANCE / LENGTH LAW -- left.len == right.len after, both
//     holding their starting length; THE PER-CHANNEL ODD LAW (held in stereo) -- every output either 0 or exactly its input, the map idempotent, an OUT-OF-PHASE master coming back STILL out of phase (the dead zone is
//     symmetric about zero, so the odd law HOLDS where the crush/tube broke it), a 1:2 master keeping its ratio on the passed samples, an identical-channel master staying identical, thresh = 0 the identity; THE
//     ATOMICITY / DEGENERATE LAW -- each refusal leaves both channels untouched and balanced, thresh = 0 the identity, count = 0 the identity ----

fn eq(got: []const i16, want: []const i16) bool {
    if (got.len != want.len) return false;
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < want.len) : (i += 1) if (got[i] != want[i]) return false;
    return true;
}

fn load_stereo(sc: *pan.StereoClip, l: []const i16, r: []const i16) !void {
    try timeline.splice(&sc.left, 0, l);
    try timeline.splice(&sc.right, 0, r);
}

fn run_selftest() !u8 {
    // 1. THE STEREO CENTER-CLIP LAW -- each channel equals ALES87's mono center_clip with the same threshold, proven side by side over one span with different per-channel samples; at t = 1000 every quiet sample
    //    (|x| ≤ 1000) silences and every louder sample passes.
    {
        var sc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&sc, &[_]i16{ 500, -1000, 999, 1001, -5000 }, &[_]i16{ 100, -50, 2500, -300, 32767 });
        try stereo_center_clip(&sc, 0, 5, 1000);

        var ml = timeline.Clip{};
        try timeline.splice(&ml, 0, &[_]i16{ 500, -1000, 999, 1001, -5000 });
        try center_clip.center_clip(&ml, 0, 5, 1000);
        var mr = timeline.Clip{};
        try timeline.splice(&mr, 0, &[_]i16{ 100, -50, 2500, -300, 32767 });
        try center_clip.center_clip(&mr, 0, 5, 1000);

        if (!eq(sc.left.samples(), ml.samples())) return error.LeftChannelWrong;
        if (!eq(sc.right.samples(), mr.samples())) return error.RightChannelWrong;
        // by hand: |500|,|−1000|,|999| ≤ 1000 silence; 1001,−5000 pass / |100|,|−50| silence; 2500,−300? |−300| ≤ 1000 silences; 2500,32767 pass.
        if (!eq(sc.left.samples(), &[_]i16{ 0, 0, 0, 1001, -5000 })) return error.LeftHandWrong;
        if (!eq(sc.right.samples(), &[_]i16{ 0, 0, 2500, 0, 32767 })) return error.RightHandWrong;
    }

    // 2. THE BALANCE / LENGTH LAW -- the channels stay equal length and each holds its starting length; a center clip writes values only. Proven at an even and an odd length.
    {
        var even = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&even, &[_]i16{ 100, -200, 3000, -4000 }, &[_]i16{ -400, 300, -200, 100 });
        try stereo_center_clip(&even, 0, 4, 1000);
        if (even.left.len != even.right.len) return error.EvenUnbalanced;
        if (even.left.len != 4) return error.EvenLength;

        var odd = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&odd, &[_]i16{ 100, -2000, 300 }, &[_]i16{ 300, -200, 100 });
        try stereo_center_clip(&odd, 0, 3, 500);
        if (odd.left.len != odd.right.len) return error.OddUnbalanced;
        if (odd.left.len != 3) return error.OddLength;
    }

    // 3a. THE PER-CHANNEL ODD LAW, the ANTISYMMETRY HOLDS -- an out-of-phase master (right the exact negation of left) center-clipped through the same threshold comes back STILL out of phase, because the dead-zone
    //     map is symmetric about zero (|−x| = |x|), so center_clip(−x) = −center_clip(x) and right = −left after. This is the mirror the crush and tube BROKE; the center clip holds it, the odd class made stereo.
    {
        var sc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&sc, &[_]i16{ 500, -3000, 900, -1200 }, &[_]i16{ -500, 3000, -900, 1200 }); // right = −left
        try stereo_center_clip(&sc, 0, 4, 1000);
        const l = sc.left.samples();
        const r = sc.right.samples();
        var i: u32 = 0;
        while (i < 4) : (i += 1) {
            if (@as(i32, r[i]) != -@as(i32, l[i])) return error.AntisymmetryBroke; // right = −left held — the odd law in stereo
        }
        // by hand: |500|,|900| ≤ 1000 silence; 3000,1200 pass. left {0,−3000,0,−1200}, right {0,3000,0,1200}.
        if (!eq(l, &[_]i16{ 0, -3000, 0, -1200 })) return error.LeftPhaseWrong;
        if (!eq(r, &[_]i16{ 0, 3000, 0, 1200 })) return error.RightPhaseWrong;
    }

    // 3b. THE PER-CHANNEL ODD LAW, output shape and idempotence -- every output on both channels is either 0 or exactly its input (the center clip never colors a passed sample), and center-clipping twice equals
    //     once (a silenced 0 stays 0, a passed sample still clears t), the map memoryless and idempotent.
    {
        const li = [_]i16{ 700, -1500, 400, -90, 4000 };
        const ri = [_]i16{ -4000, 900, -700, 33, -8 };
        var once = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&once, &li, &ri);
        try stereo_center_clip(&once, 0, 5, 1000);
        const l = once.left.samples();
        const r = once.right.samples();
        var i: u32 = 0;
        while (i < 5) : (i += 1) {
            if (l[i] != 0 and l[i] != li[i]) return error.LeftColored;
            if (r[i] != 0 and r[i] != ri[i]) return error.RightColored;
        }
        var twice = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&twice, &li, &ri);
        try stereo_center_clip(&twice, 0, 5, 1000);
        try stereo_center_clip(&twice, 0, 5, 1000);
        if (!eq(once.left.samples(), twice.left.samples())) return error.LeftNotIdempotent;
        if (!eq(once.right.samples(), twice.right.samples())) return error.RightNotIdempotent;
    }

    // 3c. THE RATIO HOLDS ON THE PASSED SAMPLES -- a 1:2 master (right twice left) is silenced together where left is quiet and passed together where left is loud, keeping the 1:2 ratio on the passed samples. Because
    //     the threshold is on magnitude, |right| = 2|left| crosses the floor with left where left ≥ t/2; the shared verdict keeps both silent or both passing.
    {
        var sc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&sc, &[_]i16{ 2000, -300, 5000, 100 }, &[_]i16{ 4000, -600, 10000, 200 }); // right = 2·left
        try stereo_center_clip(&sc, 0, 4, 1000);
        const l = sc.left.samples();
        const r = sc.right.samples();
        var i: u32 = 0;
        while (i < 4) : (i += 1) {
            if (@as(i32, r[i]) != 2 * @as(i32, l[i])) return error.RatioBroke; // passed: r = 2l; silenced: 0 = 2·0
        }
        // by hand: |2000|>1000 pass, |−300|≤1000 silence, |5000|>1000 pass, |100|≤1000 silence.
        if (!eq(l, &[_]i16{ 2000, 0, 5000, 0 })) return error.RatioLeftWrong;
        if (!eq(r, &[_]i16{ 4000, 0, 10000, 0 })) return error.RatioRightWrong;
    }

    // 3d. an identical-channel master stays identical through the center clip -- a shared dead zone on equal inputs gives equal outputs (a mono-in-stereo signal never splits).
    {
        var sc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&sc, &[_]i16{ 500, -3000, 500, -3000 }, &[_]i16{ 500, -3000, 500, -3000 });
        try stereo_center_clip(&sc, 0, 4, 1000);
        if (!eq(sc.left.samples(), sc.right.samples())) return error.IdentityChannelsSplit;
    }

    // 3e. THE SPAN DISCIPLINE -- center-clipping a sub-span leaves samples outside [start, count) exactly as they were on both channels, quiet ones among them preserved (the in-place discipline the whole suite keeps).
    {
        var sc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&sc, &[_]i16{ 100, 200, 500, 5000, 300, 400 }, &[_]i16{ -400, -300, 500, -5000, 300, 400 });
        try stereo_center_clip(&sc, 2, 2, 1000); // indices 2,3 only, both channels
        if (!eq(sc.left.samples(), &[_]i16{ 100, 200, 0, 5000, 300, 400 })) return error.LeftSpanLeaked;
        if (!eq(sc.right.samples(), &[_]i16{ -400, -300, 0, -5000, 300, 400 })) return error.RightSpanLeaked;
    }

    // 4a. THE ATOMICITY LAW, bad threshold -- a negative threshold (a magnitude is never negative) and an over-rail threshold (a floor nothing could clear) each refuse BadThreshold, both channels byte for byte
    //     untouched and still balanced.
    {
        var sc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&sc, &[_]i16{ 1, -2, 3 }, &[_]i16{ -3, 2, -1 });
        if (stereo_center_clip(&sc, 0, 3, -1)) |_| return error.NegThreshSlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadThreshold) return error.WrongNegThresh;
        if (!eq(sc.left.samples(), &[_]i16{ 1, -2, 3 })) return error.NegThreshLeftMutated;
        if (!eq(sc.right.samples(), &[_]i16{ -3, 2, -1 })) return error.NegThreshRightMutated;
        if (sc.left.len != sc.right.len) return error.NegThreshUnbalanced;

        var over = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&over, &[_]i16{ 1, 2, 3 }, &[_]i16{ 3, 2, 1 });
        if (stereo_center_clip(&over, 0, 3, @as(i32, timeline.sample_max) + 1)) |_| return error.OverThreshSlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadThreshold) return error.WrongOverThresh;
        if (!eq(over.left.samples(), &[_]i16{ 1, 2, 3 })) return error.OverThreshLeftMutated;
    }

    // 4b. THE ATOMICITY LAW, bad span -- a span past the samples refuses BadRange, both channels untouched.
    {
        var sc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&sc, &[_]i16{ 5, -6, 7 }, &[_]i16{ -7, 6, -5 });
        if (stereo_center_clip(&sc, 1, 3, 1000)) |_| return error.BadRangeSlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadRange) return error.WrongBadRange;
        if (!eq(sc.left.samples(), &[_]i16{ 5, -6, 7 })) return error.BadRangeLeftMutated;
        if (!eq(sc.right.samples(), &[_]i16{ -7, 6, -5 })) return error.BadRangeRightMutated;
    }

    // 4c. THE DEGENERATE LAW -- thresh = 0 is the identity on both channels (only x = 0 satisfies |x| ≤ 0, and it is already 0), and count = 0 is the identity on both.
    {
        var zero = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&zero, &[_]i16{ 401, -299, 703 }, &[_]i16{ -701, 201, -401 });
        try stereo_center_clip(&zero, 0, 3, 0); // identity — no dead zone
        if (!eq(zero.left.samples(), &[_]i16{ 401, -299, 703 })) return error.ZeroThreshLeftChanged;
        if (!eq(zero.right.samples(), &[_]i16{ -701, 201, -401 })) return error.ZeroThreshRightChanged;

        var noop = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&noop, &[_]i16{ 7, -8, 9 }, &[_]i16{ -7, 8, -9 });
        try stereo_center_clip(&noop, 1, 0, 1000); // empty span — identity
        if (!eq(noop.left.samples(), &[_]i16{ 7, -8, 9 })) return error.ZeroCountLeftChanged;
        if (!eq(noop.right.samples(), &[_]i16{ -7, 8, -9 })) return error.ZeroCountRightChanged;
    }

    print("GREEN ales-stereo-center-clip: the CENTER CLIPPER CARRIED INTO STEREO, ONE SHARED DEAD ZONE, opening the dead-zone corner of the stereo NONLINEAR class — center-clip a span in both channels of a master " ++
        "with the same threshold, running ALES87's proven mono center_clip on each (y = if |x| ≤ t then 0 else x, the quiet middle silenced and the loud passed unchanged, no rail edge and no saturate), so one dead " ++
        "zone lands on both speakers together. A Lotus master is a StereoClip (ALES10) whose defining invariant is that left and right hold the same length. Where ALES132's hard clip caps the LOUD extremes, the " ++
        "center clip hollows the QUIET middle — run together in stereo they keep only the band t < |x| ≤ ceil. Unlike the crush (ALES136) and tube (ALES135), which are NOT odd and break the inter-channel " ++
        "antisymmetry, the center clipper IS odd (|−x| = |x|, so center_clip(−x) = −center_clip(x)): an out-of-phase master (right = −left) comes back STILL out of phase, the odd law made stereo where the not-odd " ++
        "siblings broke it. Per channel every output is either 0 or exactly its input, the map is idempotent (twice equals once), a 1:2 master keeps its ratio on the passed samples, an identical-channel master " ++
        "stays identical, and thresh = 0 is the identity. It validates both channels once against the shared threshold and length before either is mutated (BadThreshold outside [0, sample_max], BadRange on a span " ++
        "past the samples), so a refusal never center-clips one channel and leaves the other whole; CenterClipError reused whole. The crux is four laws. THE STEREO CENTER-CLIP LAW: each channel equals ALES87's " ++
        "mono center_clip with the same threshold byte for byte. THE BALANCE / LENGTH LAW: left.len == right.len after and both hold their starting length. THE PER-CHANNEL ODD LAW: the antisymmetry HOLDS under the " ++
        "shared dead zone (an out-of-phase master staying out of phase), every output 0 or its input, the map idempotent, the ratio held on the passed samples, an identical master staying identical, thresh = 0 the " ++
        "identity. THE ATOMICITY / DEGENERATE LAW: a refusal leaves both channels untouched and balanced, thresh = 0 the identity, count = 0 the identity. Purely local — two bounded i16 Clips center-clipped " ++
        "through the proven mono center_clip, a static dead-zone threshold on instantaneous magnitude, memoryless; no real sample rate, no network, no keys, no funds, no real speaker\n", .{});
    return 0;
}

pub fn main(init: std.process.Init) !u8 {
    _ = init;
    return run_selftest();
}
